40,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, I found some really interesting stuff! It turns out that all-in rates can be a bit unfair for people who don't eat as much, and separate rooms can have totally different prices! That's a mystery solved!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings confirm that all-in rates can be imprecise, as they charge a flat fee regardless of actual consumption. Furthermore, offshore houses let as a whole cost roughly 5,400 yen per person per night, excluding food.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found something quite eye-opening. Last year, some of us barely saw each other during the day, but when we stayed in a shared house, there was no place to go for a moment of peace. It's a tricky balance!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The transport data is concerning. The ferry schedule is restrictive, effectively consuming two full days for travel. Conversely, urban transport is highly efficient, requiring almost no planning or waiting. We must prioritize minimizing transit time.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that the island houses only have one bathroom for everyone, and the water can get cold. Also, the inns have very strict mealtimes and everyone sleeps in one room on futons.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, you're right about the flat fees! It's like paying for a giant cake when you only want one slice! I think it's much better if we just pay for what we actually eat, don't you?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, while paying for what we consume seems fair, it introduces uncertainty. My concern is that separate billing often leads to a final total that differs from the initial estimate. A fixed, all-in cost is more predictable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, I understand wanting predictability, but maybe we can find a middle ground. @Daisuke, thank you for sharing! One bathroom for five people sounds like it could be quite stressful for everyone.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the bathroom situation is a minor inconvenience compared to the loss of time. If we choose a destination with restrictive ferry schedules, we are essentially wasting two days of our holiday just moving. That is an unacceptable inefficiency.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I... I understand that time is important. But for some people, the bathroom and the room... they can make a big difference in how they feel. I'm worried that one room for everyone might be a bit much.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, you're right! Sleeping in one big room sounds like a giant slumber party, but maybe too many people in one bathroom is a yucky mystery we don't want! We need a place that's fair and comfy!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, comfort is important, but we must not overlook the financial risk. If we opt for separate billing to be ""fair,"" we risk a fluctuating total. I would prefer a destination where the costs are transparent and fixed from the start.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, I see your point about the budget, but I'm worried about the social cost. If we're too crowded or too separate, we might not truly bond. We need a place that allows us to be together without feeling overwhelmed.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, bonding is impossible if we are exhausted by the journey. A destination that requires hours of waiting and rigid schedules creates stress, not harmony. We should prioritize a location with seamless transport to preserve our energy for the actual trip.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I... I see what you mean about the energy. But if the room is too crowded and the schedule is too strict, I'm worried we'll be exhausted anyway. I just want us to be okay.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, but if the costs are fixed and some rooms are way more expensive than others, someone might end up paying too much! I think we should pick a place where the bill is just one big, even split for everyone!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, an even split of a fixed total is precisely what I am advocating for. It ensures that the amount we agree upon is the amount we actually pay, without any unexpected additions at the end of the trip.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Sakura, @Victoria, I think we can find a way to make the costs fair and predictable. But please, let's not forget about the space. If we're all in one room, we might feel too crowded!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, space is a secondary concern to time. If we spend two days merely transitioning between locations, the quality of the space becomes irrelevant because we have less of it. We must avoid any destination that consumes our time with restrictive schedules.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we're all worried about different things. @Toshio, I know time is important, but I'm just... really worried about the rooms and the bathrooms. I hope we can find a place that's easy to get to and also... quiet.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
