65,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Ooh, the options are here! I think Option A sounds like a big adventure, but remember what I found? A whole house means one big bill we can just split evenly! That way, nobody gets a scary surprise! Which one do you like?","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option A is appealing because a whole-house rental allows for a fixed, predictable cost. However, we must consider the ferry schedules Toshio mentioned. Option C also offers a structured environment with meals included, which provides financial clarity.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm a bit worried about Option A. As I found, a shared house can feel crowded with no place for a moment of peace. Option B might be too separate, but Option C seems like a lovely balance!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is out of the question. The ferry schedules would waste two full days of our time. Option B is the most efficient, as urban transport requires no planning and maximizes our actual vacation time. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't think I can do Option A. One bathroom for everyone and sleeping in one room... it sounds too overwhelming. Option B sounds quiet, but I'm worried about being too alone. Maybe Option C?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Toshio, you're so grumpy about the ferry! But @Daisuke, if we do Option B, we'll have those different room prices I found, and that's not fair! Option A is the best for the wallet because it's one even split!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, I agree that a single split is the most stable approach. However, we cannot ignore the concerns of the others. Option C provides a more predictable cost than Option B, while avoiding the logistical issues of Option A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Sakura, I understand wanting a fair split, but I'm worried that Option A might make us feel too crowded. @Daisuke, I agree that Option C sounds like a wonderful way to stay connected without feeling overwhelmed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Sakura, it is not about being grumpy; it is about the value of our time. Option A is a logistical failure. Option C is acceptable, but Option B remains the most efficient choice for those who value their freedom and energy.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I... I understand. But Option B's loose plan makes me nervous. I think Option C is better because the train is easy, and having a set place for meals feels... safer. I'm worried about the room, but it's better than Option A.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, @Midori, you both like Option C! If we go there, we can still have a big group dinner and be super close! @Victoria, is Option C's money predictable too? If it is, then it's a win-win for everyone!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Midori"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, yes, Option C is quite predictable. Since meals are taken at the inn, we can establish a clear budget beforehand. It avoids the fluctuating costs of Option B and the logistical stress of Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Sakura, @Victoria, it really does seem like a win-win! Option C gives us that cozy togetherness we want, but since it's a town, we can each step out for a little peace if we need it. I'm voting for Option C!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, while I value efficiency, I can concede that Option C is a reasonable compromise. The train is far more efficient than a ferry, and it avoids the chaos of Option B's loose planning. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm glad we're all agreeing. Option C feels like the safest choice for me. It's not as crowded as Option A, and it's not as lonely as Option B. I'll vote for Option C too.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"Yay! Everyone is happy with Option C! Even if it's not a giant island adventure, a hot spring town sounds super cozy and the money will be easy to handle. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Option C provides the financial predictability I require while respecting the needs and comfort of the group. It is the most rational and harmonious choice for us all. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm so glad we could find a solution that makes everyone feel comfortable. Option C really is the perfect balance for us. I vote for Option C!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Since the consensus is clear and the transport is efficient enough to avoid the exhaustion of a ferry, I am satisfied. Option C is the most logical compromise. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm really relieved we all agree. Thank you for understanding. I think I can actually enjoy the trip if we go with this one. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
